# Selective review of the positive unary cycle clock

This review finds no mathematical repair necessary for the candidate's stated finite, supplied-model theorem. I recommend conditional analytic source acceptance of the exact body `c7a19c3acb7d731a95b97bfadc8a32e2624196d60555ac08e8e77b3ad71d1135`, subject to root's assessment. This is a review recommendation, not root acceptance, retained status, an audit, or validation of a native apparatus. The result applies to the independently prepared specified one-excitation clock and a finite supplied full-H waveform. It does not cover arbitrary clock inputs, a fixed clock strength as accuracy improves, an ordinary open path, or a wholly nearest-neighbor apparatus.

The substantive content checked is the full-phase, retained-clock prepared-map estimate, including its noncommuting data background, strict sampling guard, two outside-band comparisons, sine dispersion, explicit finite choices, physical supports and term budgets, energy/covariance ledger, and application to the existing full-output words. The optional clock-preparation circuit is also sound under its separately stated addressable-control, clean-vacuum, timing and drift-removal or exact-compensation assumptions. Those assumptions remain supplied; they are not conclusions of the autonomous evolution theorem. Reduced timing and read-energy bounds retain their stated sector and operation hypotheses.

