## 3. Persistent H, signed program and exact physical clock

Candidate sections 1–3 correctly preserve the original H during every pulse and wait. The waveform is chronological evolution of H+V0(t), not a word in isolated V pulses and not an interaction picture with H silently removed. The inherited certificate is an operator-norm statement for the complete supplied waveform; its actual duration T includes recurrence waits. Keeping H in the diagonal Fourier blocks works even when its norm is large or it fails to commute with every control. The scalar coefficient of the literal data Hamiltonian remains in this full evolution. The finite data/reference theorem itself is not restricted to the Gauss code.

Positive Fejér convolution has degree R, is normalized, and preserves Hermiticity and the pointwise program norm bound c. It also preserves the bounded-variation translation inequality. The cosine-moment argument gives the stated first-moment allowance, and convolution plus the full-circle variation estimate bounds its restriction to [0,T]. Grouping by actual supports before convolution is legitimate. Each finite coefficient in (6), including q=0 and scalar pulse parts, is retained. Positivity of the smoothing kernel does not make the signed data program positive.

For a clock pair, define C = sigma_j^- − i sigma_(j+1)^-. The physical numerator in (7) is C* C, so b_j=C* C/(2a). Its vacuum, one-excitation and two-excitation blocks have the claimed eigenvalues. Thus b_j is positive on the full pair space, and the sum is positive on all clock sectors without diagonalizing the many-qubit Hamiltonian. On the one-excitation space, each position receives two diagonal half-contributions, producing exactly I/a. With the displayed positive-exponent Fourier convention, T_L has eigenvalue exp(−2 pi i k/L), hence i(T_L−T_L*)/(2a) has eigenvalue +sin(2 pi k/L)/a. The orientation and positive scalar are both essential.

The clock is a cycle with an actual physical closing bond. It has L physical qubits, not a log L binary register. The sampled program commutes with clock number, so the exact one-excitation subspace is reducing for the nominal dynamics. The norm c for its program is valid there; Lc is the safe corresponding full-space bound. H_aut need not be positive because the clock vacuum retains H. These distinctions are correctly stated.

## 4. Strict compression, both buffers and the general error bound

The finite Fourier sum in (12) is exact. If |k|,|l|≤B and |q|≤R, then |q+l−k|≤2B+R. The strict condition L>2B+R leaves only the zero multiple of L and proves ordinary Toeplitz compression. A weak inequality at equality permits a boundary harmonic and is not interchangeable. The candidate's preserved alias example is a valid counterexample to that weakened interface, not a refutation of cycle clocks.

The continuum comparison is justified on the standard self-adjoint momentum domain because V_R is bounded and H acts on a finite separate factor. In the interaction picture of H+P, each insertion still shifts momentum by at most R; conjugation by H changes its data matrix, not its Fourier support or norm. Every prefix through order r stays within K+rR=B. The finite compression therefore has the same word coefficients through that order, with both tails bounded by E_r. This yields 2E_r, not one unpriced tail.

The ring-to-sine-band comparison is a separate argument. Its free sine phases agree on the selected band. The same prefix restriction and B<L/2 prevent a modular wrap in the coefficients being identified. This contributes another 2E_r. Consequently the total 4E_r in (18) and (19) is justified. The proof does not assert that all paths ending inside the band stayed there; it uses every prefix. It also does not identify sampling of an arbitrary infinite Fourier vector with an isometry. Only the common finite-band vectors and the finite free packet are compared through exact isometries.

Within the band, |sin z−z|≤|z|^3/6 gives delta_B. Both generators are self-adjoint finite matrices with the same H and V_B, so unitary Duhamel gives t delta_B without a factor exp(hT). This is valid for the full noncommuting data matrix. The characteristic solution then compares U_y(t) with U_0(t) by the operator Duhamel inequality and the full-circle variation bound. Squaring and integrating against the actual flat-packet density gives d_K; replacing the smoothed waveform costs d_R. This proves the stated linear-comparator bound.

The physical clock has the scalar I/a and a sine dispersion relation, so its free packet is not exactly the continuum translation. The candidate preserves exp(−it/a) in the operator comparison and pays the further T delta_K to use the actual free clock. I find the resulting bound

    d_a = d_R + d_K + 4 E_r(T) + T(delta_B + delta_K)

valid uniformly for 0≤t≤T at the stated prepared-isometry interface. Tensoring an arbitrary passive reference leaves the operator norm unchanged; purification and the pure-state trace inequality give the claimed joint trace bound min(2,2d_a). This is stronger than a clock-discarded or local-observable claim, but only for the specified initially independent packet. Approximate final decoupling is not exact clock return, stopping, reset or catalytic reuse.

## 5. Effective choices, optional preparation and physical resources

The sufficient integer choices are consistent. R=K≥2(B_var S/b)^2 controls both smoothing terms. With n=r+1≥6cT, the factorial bound and a geometric tail give E_r≤2^(1−n); n≥log2(32/b) then makes 4E_r≤b/4. The second L inequality is exactly the rearrangement of T(delta_B+delta_K)≤b/4. Rounding L upward to a multiple of four preserves both inequalities. These finite choices use certified upper estimates and strict integer slack, not a decision oracle for equality of arbitrary computable reals.

The source explicitly assumes effective finite matrix/interval input and certified positive tolerance/time information for an algorithmic claim. Without those premises it claims finite existence, not effective synthesis from noncomputable data. The method may be expensive. As a=S/L shrinks, physical hopping strengths and local clock budgets grow. The background H and supplied physical duration have not been rescaled to hide that cost.

The optional preparation addition in the exact historical diff is correct. Starting with a single head at site zero, the two columns of G_j in section 3 are orthonormal because beta_j is real and |alpha_j|^2+beta_j^2=1. Acting on the positive residual r_j produces the prescribed complex z_j and a positive remaining residual. Earlier amplitudes encounter |00> on subsequent pairs and remain unchanged. Induction followed by the final one-site phase produces the full complex target state, not only its populations. A zero residual means all later amplitudes vanish, so that identity branch is valid. For finite integer L, the needed zero tests are on algebraic root-of-unity expressions, not general computable-real tests.

There are at most L+1 gates including initial X and the final phase. A Hermitian logarithm with norm at most pi supplies the stated upper duration at an arbitrary addressed control cap J_p, and a telescoping operator bound gives the stated 2(L+1)eta_p trace cost. This is conditional on the additional external control/timing and clock-preparation drift removal or exact compensation. Data must arrive after preparation or have its earlier evolution charged. The source makes those obligations explicit; the preparation is not a new autonomous, native or efficient supply result.

The square-perimeter coordinates provide distinct sites outside the original 64-cube data box. All clock bonds, including the closing edge, are ordinary nearest-neighbor edges. The data-program coupling n_j tensor V_(j,X) has at most three sites, but its range grows. The safe Manhattan diameter 190+L/2 and supplied enlarged-box spectator convention are consistent. This does not change the original H supports or seam terms.

The support count uses 262144 box vertices and 774144 ordinary edges. Since the unsmoothed waveform is serial, the sum of supported block norms is bounded by c at each time. Positive convolution preserves that sum bound. Thus each clock site's whole-term budget is at most 2/a+c. At a data site the exact discrete quadrature a sum_j F_R(x_j−t)=1 is valid because R<L; applying the triangle inequality before the sample sum yields ell+c t_i/a. The distinction from a global one-excitation norm and from the old binary clock cap ell+7c is necessary and correctly retained. The loose description count prices Lu supported samples, u(2R+1) Fourier matrices and L physical clock factors. It is a formula specifying finite resources, not an emitted large parameter table or an executed apparatus.

## 6. Initial energy moments, optional full positivity and errors

For the exact flat real momentum packet, sine oddness makes the free-clock mean exactly 1/a. The finite cosine sum gives the displayed variance and the inequality |sin(kp)|≤|kp| gives its upper bound. The total-energy variance must use Xi=sum_j p_j V_j^2. Replacing Xi by Vbar^2 would remove genuine sampling fluctuations.

The clock–program covariance cancellation is particular to this packet and its no-alias regime. In each q contribution, the involution k↦−k−q preserves the allowed pair set and reverses sin(kp)+sin((k+q)p), while the data matrix A_q is independent of k. This proves cancellation before any choice of rho. Product preparation separately cancels clock–H covariance. It does not cancel the H–V covariance. The exact formula (28) retains that term, and the norm of H+V on the reducing sector yields the safe standard-deviation bound. No property of a reduced channel alone is used to infer total variance.

The ledger −Delta<K_C>=Delta<H>+Delta<V> follows from the conserved mean of the actual static H_aut, and |Delta<V>|≤2c holds on the invariant sector. It is not a branchwise work law or an assertion that clock energy must decrease. The optional full positive model adds hI and cN_C. H+hI and each n_j tensor(cI+V_j) are positive on all sectors, so it really is positive there. Adding hN_C instead would leave the vacuum defect. On the prepared sector its extra scalar h+c is paid in phase and mean; the variance is unchanged. These reserves are supplied engineering choices, not a derived physical energy identification.

The structured perturbation row bound eta_d+2eta_h is valid for Hermitian number-preserving onsite/hopping errors. Supported sample errors add eta_V, not a bound on each coefficient without summing its incidences. The full-space norm estimate is separately required for arbitrary Hermitian errors that can leave the sector. Compressed P1 E P1 alone is insufficient. The source explicitly makes that distinction and separately requires any claimed actual positivity/support conservation.

Uniform resource preparation trace error is transported by contractivity even if it leaks. Its energy and variance consequences then require full operator norms: L/a for K_C and h+L/a+Lc for nominal H_aut, or 2h+L/a+2Lc for the optional positive model. The factor 3M^2 in a safe variance continuity bound follows by bounding the second moment and the difference of squared means. Sector norms may replace these only when both states are certified in that sector.

The timing paragraph is expressly for sector-preserving evolution. The reduced-state estimate follows because the partial trace of the free-clock commutator vanishes even for correlated states. It must not be reused with c for an arbitrary leaked actual state whose program only has full-space norm Lc. Equation (32)'s word “applicable” therefore matters: use the restricted timing statement under its hypotheses, or charge a justified full-space/actual-generator bound. I read this as an explicit limit already imposed by the source, not a missing universal leakage theorem or a requested mathematical repair.

## 7. Target composition and readout semantics

At terminal time the full-H waveform certificate can be added in operator norm to the clock prepared-map bound. Preparation, calibration and physical terminal-instrument errors then compose by triangle inequality and complete trace contraction. This is valid with unknown data/reference states and returned dirty factors because the underlying word interface is global. The neutral word still requires its stated clean active input; binary admission does not assume an active input already in K. Its PASS and FAIL blocks remain unnormalized. Normalizing a rare branch would be a different and unproved guarantee.

The flag dephasing statement also has a precise hypothesis. If it leaves H invariant, it leaves both H and the clock-only mean unchanged, so only the program expectation changes, at most 2c on the invariant sector. A data operation that changes H needs the larger 2(h+c) bound. No unconditional zero-energy-read claim is made; no postselected energy bound follows by dividing (34) by a small probability. The supplied terminal map is not a constructed physical reader, finite read-time device, stopped clock or permanent record store.

## 8. The independent finite control and what it establishes

The single new control source is `selected_control/exact_cycle_control.py`, SHA `6d7d651bd20cf2d4643d355518a6cf3d1b2a35e720068ea35bd6450c53341f2f`. Its actual stdout/RESULT identity is `fac4e7e773de9a65a2de35adfa4db1f21536372bbbdf0eca0f598e31c0d64df5`; the full actual command, Python/platform, executed source, timestamps, exit zero and empty stderr are retained in `control_run01/`. There was one scientific execution and no scientific rerun.

It uses exact rational coefficients in Q[z]/Phi_16 and Q[z]/Phi_12. The site-basis physical edges and sampled program are constructed separately from the ordinary momentum matrix, and an explicit unnormalized Fourier matrix has F*F=L I. The common synthetic input is H=Z+I/3 and V(x)=[X cos(2 omega x)+Z sin(omega x)]/4, S=16, T=4, K=1, R=2, r=2, B=5. The valid grid is L=16; L=12 is the deliberate equality/alias mutation with the same S. This differs in arithmetic, representation and fixture from the later-read author's floating propagation case.

| Selected issue | Exact observed result | Limit |
|---|---|---|
| Ordinary sampling and strict guard | No compression difference at L=16. At L=12=2B+R, four matrix entries differ; the row −5, column +5 data block is X/8. | Concrete failure of the weakened guard, not a full-parameter proof by enumeration. |
| Physical hopping orientation | Correct sine diagonal obtained exactly. Reversal produces 14 and 10 nonzero differences on the two grids; the L=12 k=1 difference is −3/4. | Phase convention is fixed by the explicit site operator and Fourier map. |
| Every-prefix cutoff | Prepared generator powers agree through orders 0,1,2. At order 3 there are 12 nonzero differences; the mode +7 block is X/512, independently equal to the unique three-highest-shift product. | A formal coefficient witness, not a measured finite-time or diamond-norm lower bound. |
| Noncommuting background | The second-order difference between exp[−it(H+W)] and exp(−itH)exp(−itW) is [H,W]/2, with 24 nonzero entries and site-zero block [[0,1/4],[−1/4,0]]. | Detects a false factorization; does not perform a new recurrence compilation. |
| Paid clock scalar | The paid-clock map minus the offset-omitted map has first-order prepared amplitude −iI/a. | Density operators alone cannot test a common phase; the operator comparison can. |
| Closing edge | Removing the entire positive closing bond, including its diagonal contributions, has nonzero exact action on the packet; its norm is 1 at a=1. | No ordinary-open-path impossibility theorem or time-uniform lower bound. |
| Positivity and sector domain | Exact C* C factorization and local spectrum {0,0,1,1} at a=1. P1 X_0 P1=0 although X_0 P1 has two nonzero entries. Wrong hN_C reserve leaves energy −1 on vacuum clock/negative-data vector, whereas hI gives 0. | Local domain controls, not a two-site transport cycle or dense global sector test. |

All wrong-interface outputs are retained, not reclassified as program failures. The arithmetic represents the intended roots exactly; no floating root or exponential integrator is used. This finite algebra supports the named load-bearing distinctions. It does not evaluate the complete general error bound, implement the 1344-qubit literal data model, prepare the proposed clock, certify experimental energy, or replace the analytic proof.

## 9. Author evidence, histories and failures

The author's one science run at 14:20:04.684317–14:20:06.388373 UTC uses a two-dimensional noncommuting H and a 128-site clock. Its executed source SHA is `04b1ea8a38a6f15c2c20ee89ac81c1b78be5cc7bfae045b409c5b515a0d278a9`; stdout SHA is `826d771bd46917e7a53377571b6290b6d47a2cb4951b2d8eaffea22cea636e5b`. The complete source, output and receipt were inspected, not rerun. The actual-free and linear-comparator errors are about 0.0154682 and 0.0157984 against bounds 0.4891993 and 0.4841528. Its reversed-hop and omitted-H mutants exceed the same bound. The Bell-reference result and direct/formula variance comparison are finite floating corroboration. The exact geometric rational bound 9/246250 is a valid upper bound for its infinite tail, rather than a truncated positive sum. The nonzero H–V covariance and Xi−Vbar^2 witness match the analytic distinctions. None of these numbers is an interval proof or a general theorem check.

The candidate preserves its 30,708-byte first complete proof and exact preparation/energy correction. The current 33,019-byte body was read fully; the old full body was preserved and its complete diff reconstructed, not counted as a second fresh full proof read. Both current additions were checked above. The four author bookkeeping runs and one science run all have actual exit-zero receipts; no author's failed science run is claimed or concealed. The author's local 4-by-4 positivity fixture does not by itself fix the chiral sign under an unstated tensor ordering; its ring test and this review's explicit C* C/site-basis convention supply that separate check. This is a limitation of what that tiny fixture proves, not a defect in the displayed mathematical operator.

This review preserves its own failures too. Before the first preassessment seal, the control plan's unnormalized site-map Gram and momentum-map Gram were distinguished by an exact saved wording diff. The expected missing-directory probe and actual preparation actions remain in `PRESEAL_TOOL_ACTIONS.json`. The first candidate-exposure record used a wrong original-path metadata string caused by resolving a lexical Path('.') parent; the displayed snapshot path, body identity and exposure time were correct. The complete original record remains unchanged, with a separate exact correction record.

At 15:08:58 UTC the first new source binder failed because it incorrectly assumed all five author runs used the generic recorder. The selected science run actually used its distinct `RUN_SELECTED.py`, already preserved in its raw run directory. The failed binder source, exit-one receipt, full traceback and nine partial source copies remain untouched. A new binder version changes only the recorder choice and allows already-present exact partial copies; the complete diff and repair receipt are saved. The successful identity-only run at 15:10:06–07 UTC then checked the intended closure. This was a reviewer bookkeeping error, not a candidate scientific defect or a reason to rerun science.

A repeated aggregate display of old parent exposure metadata was truncated during this review. It was not treated as a completed new read of that metadata or as proof coverage; the relevant route pin list and actual load-bearing source ranges were displayed separately, and prior complete exact coverage is explicitly identified. All actual scientific sources and streams relied on here were read without relying on that truncated display. Historical parent discovery/capture failures and source-exposure limits remain intact in the complete nested archives. No search, failure history or identity count is repurposed as mathematical acceptance.

## 10. Root decision and remaining scope

The stated finite theorem survives the selected challenges. Its sufficient resources, scalar phases, reducing-sector assumptions, supplied full-H certificate and actual T are mutually consistent. I request no mathematical body change. Root may assess this exact source for conditional analytic acceptance; publication, canonical parent bindings, retained audit and any later construction remain separate decisions.

The unresolved tasks outside this source are physical supply of the engineered couplings, clean coherent packet, arbitrary addressed preparation controls or compensation, calibrated signed program and original H, observation timing and terminal reader. A fixed common strength, whole-apparatus nearest-neighbor locality, open-path replacement, efficient scaling, all-clock-state transport, repeated reuse, native matter/photon/rotor realization and physical identification of the chosen positive reserve are not established. Nothing in the exact finite witnesses supports a universal no-go for those tasks. No editable prompt, axiom, checkpoint, canonical or Git file was changed; no model/effort change or new agent was used.
